    "title": "Mandatory access control disabled",
    "desc": "A program turned off SELinux or AppArmor - setenforce 0 / Permissive, an aa-disable / aa-teardown / aa-complain, a systemctl stop/disable of apparmor, or an edit of /etc/selinux/config to SELINUX=disabled. The mandatory-access-control layer is what confines a service to what it is allowed to touch, so switching it off removes a containment boundary before acting (MITRE T1562.001). disable_logging and disable_firewall cover the logging and network defenses; this covers the MAC layer.",
